  data:  # 9c6b
    kind: invariant  # 9c6b
    title: "the test slicer has no data-file edge, so changing an io_primitives catalogue selects ~1 test file for a change ~1,600 tests depend on"  # 9c6b
    status: violated  # 9c6b
    priority: 2  # 9c6b
    parent:  # 9c6b
    tags:  # 9c6b
    - testing  # 9c6b
    - ci  # 9c6b
    - io_boundary  # 9c6b
    isbefore: []  # 9c6b
    duplicate_of: []  # 9c6b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9c6b
    pr_ref:  # 9c6b
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-27 while shipping WI-bupor's rust.yaml rows.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT. Changing\npackages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/io_primitives/rust.yaml -- the\nRust I/O primitive catalogue -- produced this manifest:\n\n    # Changed files: 6\n    # Changed source files: 0\n    # Selected tests: 1\n\nONE test file, and only because a NEW test file was added in the same commit.\nHad the rows been added without a new test, the selection would have been\nZERO. Meanwhile 19 test files (1,648 tests) read that catalogue, and they run\nin 27 seconds -- so this is not a budget tradeoff, it is a missing edge.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. `hypergumbo slice --files` walks Python imports. A YAML data\nfile has no import edge to the modules that read it, so the slicer classifies\nit as \"not a source file\" and the whole dependency fan-out is invisible. The\nsame shape applies to every non-Python input the production code loads at\nruntime: io_primitives/*.yaml, taint catalogues, overlays, and any future\ndata-driven registry.\n\nWHY IT IS A SAFETY-NET DEFECT RATHER THAN A NUISANCE. The manifest is what CI\nruns for a PR (ci.yml extracts it with `grep \"^packages/\"`). CI's CORE_CHANGED\nescape hatch force-runs the full suite for seven named .py files -- sketch.py,\nslice.py, cli.py, ir.py, all_analyzers.py, base.py, registry.py -- and a\ncatalogue is not among them. So a PR that changes what the tool CLASSIFIES AS\nI/O gets a one-file gate. Full-suite.yml catches it after merge, twice daily,\nwhich means dev can be red for up to twelve hours from a change whose blast\nradius was knowable at selection time.\n\nWORKED AROUND, NOT FIXED, in the WI-bupor PR: the manifest was manually\nextended to the 19 catalogue-exercising files, with a comment saying why. A\nmanual extension is not a fix -- it depends on the author noticing, and the\nauthor only noticed here because the \"1 test file\" line looked implausible for\nthe change that had just been made.\n\nTWO CANDIDATE REMEDIES, neither adjudicated here:\n  * teach the slicer a data-file edge -- map a non-Python file to the modules\n    that reference its path or directory, which for io_primitives is a single\n    well-known loader (_CATALOG_DIR in io_boundary.py).\n  * extend CI's CORE_CHANGED list to cover data directories, which is cruder\n    but needs no slicer work and fails safe."  # 9c6b
    fields:  # 9c6b
      statement: "A change to a non-Python input the production code loads at runtime must select the tests that exercise it. Changing io_primitives/rust.yaml reports 'changed source files: 0' and selects only tests added in the same commit, while 19 test files read that catalogue."  # 9c6b
      root_cause: "hypergumbo slice --files walks Python imports; a YAML data file has no import edge to its loader, so its dependents are invisible to selection. CI's CORE_CHANGED force-full-suite escape names seven .py files and no data directory."  # 9c6b
- op: discuss  # 6ee1
  at: '2026-08-27T07:23:09Z'  # 6ee1
  by: agent  # 6ee1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6ee1
  clock: 2  # 6ee1
  nonce: 6ee1  # 6ee1
  message: "THE DOCUMENTED WORKAROUND FOR THIS ITEM HAS NEVER ONCE WORKED, and the item\nshould not be closed on it. Recorded 2026-08-27.\n\nThe workaround in circulation was \"manually extend .ci/affected-tests.txt with\nthe tests that actually exercise the changed catalogue, then commit it\".\nExtending it works. KEEPING it did not: `auto-pr` re-runs `smart-test\n--manifest` during the push and, if the regenerated manifest differs from the\ncommitted one, `git add`s it into an amended commit -- an unconditional\noverwrite that replaces the author's wider list with the slicer's narrow one.\n\nMEASURED, not inferred. Found by reading a CI log that said \"1 selected files\"\nfor a commit whose own manifest listed twenty. Checked across three merged\ncatalogue PRs (#565, #567, #568) plus their pre-rebase commits: EVERY ONE\nshipped a 1-file manifest. So every catalogue PR in this campaign had CI\nvalidate roughly one test file while the agent's notes recorded a working\n19-file extension. The overwrite is invisible from the author's side -- extend,\ncommit correctly, replaced afterwards -- which is why it survived this long.\n\nFIXED AS OF de8403b14c + 2d7819f4ac (not by closing this item). auto-pr's regen\nis now a UNION: it MAY ADD a newly-affected test (its real job -- catching a\nstale manifest) and can never DROP one. Paths that no longer exist are still\ndropped so a deleted test cannot be resurrected, and auto-pr now prints how\nmany committed entries it kept that the slicer did not select, so a future\nnarrowing is visible instead of silent. Same shape and same remedy as\nWI-buhov's `.ops` overwrite; `_manifest_union` sits beside\n`_ops_union_restore_file` in scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh.\n\nTHIS ITEM REMAINS violated. The root cause is untouched: the slicer still has\nno data-file -> test edge, so a change to io_primitives/*.yaml still slices to\nroughly ONE test file. What changed is only that a HAND extension now survives\nthe push. The real fix is still one of the two originally filed -- teach the\nslicer a data-file edge, or extend CI's CORE_CHANGED list to data directories.\nUntil then the manual extension is load-bearing, and it is now durable.\n\nTWO CAUTIONS FOR WHOEVER TAKES THE ROOT CAUSE, both paid for today:\n * THE MANIFEST IS SECTIONED. CI reads everything after\n   \"# === SELECTED_TESTS ===\" as the test list and the region above it as\n   CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES. Entries are \"tests/...\" OR\n   \"packages/<pkg>/tests/...\" depending on what was selected, so a path-prefix\n   match is NOT a valid reader. The first cut of the fix selected with\n   `grep '^packages/'` and would have written an EMPTY test list for the very\n   95-entry manifest that motivated it -- CI would have run nothing and\n   reported success. Strictly worse than the defect.\n * THE SAME MISTAKE THEN SURVIVED IN THE REPORTING PATH one PR later: the\n   \"kept N\" counter still used the prefix, came out 0 on both sides, and the\n   line that makes a narrowing visible silently never printed. One fact, two\n   homes, second one wins. Section-reading now has exactly one implementation\n   (`_manifest_selected_tests`) that both callers use."  # 6ee1
